UP|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|As you noticed, North can afford to overtake the club. He needs to count the club suit. I started with @CAJ doubleton. Dummy had 4. That leaves West with @C10xx. So overtaking and playing the @CQ would drop the 10. Further, at trick 7, North can make the defense easier by winning the @H10,|
PG| ***** 41 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|This was another example of how it is easy to mis-defend.|
PG| ***** 42 ***** |


